+# Receipts stopped
+
+For the volunteer on call when members report no receipts for their pantry orders. Brings receipt emails flowing
+again; while the worker is down, confirmed pantry orders queue silently and members get no proof of payment. Written
+after it happened twice, on 2024-09-14 and once before, each time leaving members waiting until the one volunteer
+who knew the fix was free. Owner: the payments volunteers.
+
+## Before you begin
+
+- SSH access to the server running `larder-worker`.
+- `psql` access to the `larder` database.
+
+## Steps
+
+1. Check the worker: `systemctl status larder-worker`.
+
+   Expected: `active (running)`. If it instead shows `inactive (dead)`, the worker has stopped; the deploy script
+   only restarts the web app, so a deploy can leave the worker down without anyone noticing until receipts stop.
+2. Count the queued jobs: `psql larder -c "select status, count(*) from procrastinate_jobs group by status"`.
+
+   Expected: a number of jobs `todo`, confirming the backlog that built up while the worker was down.
+3. Start the worker: `sudo systemctl start larder-worker`.
+
+   Expected: `systemctl status larder-worker` now shows `active (running)`.
+4. Re-run the count query from step 2 every minute or so.
+
+   Expected: `todo` drops to 0, at roughly 40 jobs a minute. A few jobs left in `failed` are expected: those are
+   receipts for bounced emails, where the member has no valid address, and are not a sign of a problem.
+
+## If it fails
+
+If the worker dies again right away, collect its recent log: `journalctl -u larder-worker -n 50`, and ask the
+payments volunteers in the pantry's chat, as in [gateway timeouts](gateway-timeouts.md).
